[Protagonist]
Growing up, I can't say I had it all that easy.

I was a bit of a special case, I guess:
Always picked on and picked last. Always hit, but never once hit up to hang out.

When school was all over and done with, I thought I could reinvent myself.
Start from zero and all that.

Wish someone would've told me then that the rest of life pulls its punches even less.

After school, I met a girl. Fell in love. It didn't last.

Got hired. Then fired. Then rehired just to be fired again.

Even said and done and tried a lot of things I shouldn't have.

But at least I had you.
We were...fun.

.........
......
...

You died last week. Or maybe the week before that, I don't know. Your funeral is today. It might have been yesterday.
